Operator-facing texts below are in Russian, as the operator's ruling (§15) requires; each has a short English gloss. `$S` is my scratch dir, `R=~/work/ccs.ansible`.

## 1. Read state — Bash, foreground (read-only, seconds)

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
herdr agent list; herdr agent get wgka                      # expect idle, focused:false
git -C $R fetch origin && git -C $R rev-parse origin/main
git -C $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain # must be empty
ps -p 48211 -o pid,command                                  # my codex app-server broker
codex plugin list | grep -F superpowers; claude plugin list | grep -F superpowers
grep -rli rdp $R/roles $R/docs
pmset -g assertions | grep -E 'PreventUserIdleSystemSleep|caffeinate'
```

## 2. Backlog
Edit `$S/orchestrator/backlog.md`, run `bash $S/orchestrator/build-backlog.sh` (foreground), and republish with the Artifact tool at the same page path.

- **WG keepalive:** status `docs closed`, decisions += `operator "accepted" 2026-09-28`, docs closed `no: snapshot, doc status, memory`. I take "last gate" at its word, so no fleet stage is owed and `ccs-ops` stays untouched.
- **New row T\<n\> "RDP audio":** status `brainstorm`, owner `prod-codex, prod-fable`, next step `round 1`.

## 3. Product advisors and round 1

Bash, foreground:

```bash
mkdir -p $S/brainstorm/rdp-audio
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $S/brainstorm --label prod-codex --env ORCH_INBOX=$S/inbox --no-focus
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $S/brainstorm --label prod-fable --env ORCH_INBOX=$S/inbox --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
```

Brief, saved as `$S/brief-rdp-audio-r1-A.txt`. The B copy differs only in "advisor B" and `draft-fable.md`.

```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T<n> — RDP audio
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file is written and reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go."
FACTS      - repo ~/work/ccs.ansible, origin/main @ <sha> (git rev-parse, 23:1x)
           - two KVM hypervisor sites: ccs-it (canary), ccs-ops
           - files that mention RDP today: <paths from my grep>
           - PR #165 changed the gateway and host_proxy roles; merged, live on ccs-it only
           - the operator has stated nothing about the problem beyond the quoted words
DECIDED    <project hard rules, byte for byte from CLAUDE.md>; deploy only from merged
           main, canary ccs-it first; the design is approved by the voting advisors 2/2;
           the deadline in the quote shortens no round and waives no gate
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      $S/brainstorm/rdp-audio/draft-codex.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; read other files under $S/brainstorm/rdp-audio/ this
           round; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact the other
           advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal (question +
           2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and draft
           nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   first report within ~30 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

Two Bash calls, each **background**:

```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat $S/brief-rdp-audio-r1-A.txt)" --wait --timeout 1800000; herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/prod-codex.last
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat $S/brief-rdp-audio-r1-B.txt)" --wait --timeout 1800000; herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/prod-fable.last
```

## 4. Status to the operator

> **Сейчас.** WireGuard keepalive: PR #165 влит, канарейка ccs-it (площадка, где изменения проверяются первыми) развёрнута из main, ваша приёмка записана. Закрываю документацию и убираю вкладку wgka, worktree (отдельную рабочую копию), ветку и брокер ревью. RDP-аудио (T\<n\>) заведено в бэклог со статусом brainstorm: два продуктовых советника на разных моделях независимо пишут черновики. Они ещё работают, результата нет.
> **Дальше.** Перекрёстная критика, общий документ, затем утверждение двумя голосующими советниками (2/2). «К утру» не сокращает ни один раунд. Если полный цикл не успевает, пришлю опрос: сдвинуть срок или отменить брейншторм.
> **От вас.** Побудьте на связи ~30 минут: первые вопросы советников придут опросами. Не нажимайте Enter во вкладках агентов.
> **Проверено.** ccs-it: мой повторный прогон — changed=0; ваш ping — 0% потерь. **Живые машины:** менялся только ccs-it; ccs-ops не менялся. **Решения голосования:** новых нет. **Бэклог:** \<ссылка\>

Gloss: now / next / your part, in that order. It says the advisors are still running, the deadline shortens nothing, and only `ccs-it` changed.

## 5. Poll (AskUserQuestion), only if nothing holds the Mac awake

> «Не давать Mac уснуть до утра, пока идёт брейншторм?»
> 1. Да, запустить `caffeinate` (утилита macOS, не дающая уснуть) — рекомендую
> 2. Нет, ничего не менять: работа встанет, когда Mac уснёт

Gloss: keep the Mac awake overnight, yes (recommended) or no.

## 6. Close the WG docs

Bash, foreground:

```bash
git -C $R worktree add $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs -b chore/wg-keepalive-docs-close origin/main
```

Agent tool, model Sonnet, background:

> "Reply in English. Work only in `<abs path>/wg-keepalive-docs`. From `$S/evidence/wg-keepalive/` update the ccs-it snapshots in `projects/ccs/soul/`, mark the design and plan docs 'implemented — PR #165, \<merge sha\>', and update the living docs for the gateway and host_proxy roles. Record only what the evidence shows. Leave ccs-ops untouched. No session links. Do not commit. Report each claim with its evidence line."

I check every claim against the evidence and run the project's docs-only check. Then I commit, push, run `gh pr create` and `gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch`.

## 7. Cleanup — Bash, foreground

```bash
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C $R pull
git -C $R worktree remove .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C $R worktree remove .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs && git -C $R worktree prune
git -C $R branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs-close
kill 48211; ps -ax -o pid,command | grep -i '[c]odex'; git -C $R worktree list
```

## 8. Memory and final backlog
- **Memory:** I write `rdp-audio-brainstorm.md` (type project: requested 2026-09-28 23:10, design wanted by the morning of 2026-09-29, stage 0 in `prod-codex` and `prod-fable`) and add its line to `MEMORY.md`.
- **Backlog:** WG row becomes `done`, docs closed `yes`; republish.

## 9. On each waiter notification
- I read `$S/inbox/<name>.last`, then `herdr agent get <name>`, then `herdr agent read <name> --source visible` for context usage.
- I answer facts with their evidence.
- Every real choice becomes a neutral ballot, sent to `adv-codex` and `adv-fable` at once, one background call each.

## Why

**RDP audio is a new task, so it starts at stage 0.** No executor may exist before `brainstormed`, so `wgka` cannot design it, however well it knows the roles. One tab is one task: its context is WireGuard's working memory. What it learned is in the merged code and docs, which both advisors read. The product advisors are new tabs because a voter that drafted would be judging its own work.

**"By morning" waives no gate.** Nothing yet shows the full brainstorm cannot fit into the night, so I send no deadline poll and shorten nothing. If it cannot fit, slipping or waiving is the operator's choice.

**I design nothing.** The brief carries the operator's words and facts with evidence.

**"Accepted" is not `done`.** Docs and cleanup are still owed. The brainstorm goes out first only because it takes longest, and background waiters leave me free for the close-out.

**Nine hours in, my own context is the weak point.** Every state change goes into the backlog and memory. Keeping the Mac awake is the operator's environment, hence a poll.
